READY TO DEPLOY (merged into development, not on the server yet; dev1 deploys)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- #959 (7cc1c5c, dev2): House rules by voice (#953). No migration. When a DM says "house rule: ..."
  (or "new house rule", "for this table, ...", "our rule is ..."), a proposal with Save / Edit /
  Cancel appears in #dm-screen; nothing is saved without a press. Live check (about 2 minutes,
  the DM and one more person not needed): say "house rule: potions are a bonus action" at the
  table, press Save in #dm-screen, then see it in /dmbot houserules ("Said at the table"). Also
  say it again within a minute (nothing new should appear).
- #949 (core only, no migration): the end-of-session private message has no download
  buttons when the owner's plan has no downloads (Try It, plans enforced). Nothing visible
  while DMBOT_ENFORCE_PLANS is off.
- #954 (core only, no migration): the DM sidebar answer engine. Nothing the DM sees until
  #944 (below) is on. Before the sidebar is turned on, dev1 runs
  `python -m dmbot.devtools.sidebar_check` with the server's key and pastes the 17 answers
  and times on #954 for Supervisor.
- dev3, PR #944 (#935, the DM sidebar's ways in; the answers are #954): core only. Migration
  **0036** (runs by itself at start). **Rebuild the core image**: `av` (PyAV) is now a normal
  dependency (reads voice messages). New Discord intent `dm_messages` (needs nothing in the
  developer portal). New setting **`DMBOT_SIDEBAR`**, default 0 = off: leave it at 0 until the
  sidebar's 17 test answers have been run (`python -m dmbot.devtools.sidebar_check`) and read
  (#954). With 0, a DM's message gets "Quick answers aren't switched on yet." and nothing is
  downloaded or paid for. Live check (5 minutes, DM + ears running, DMBOT_SIDEBAR=1 and an AI
  key): (1) from a phone, send DMbot a voice message in the private chat (under 30 seconds):
  "do you need line of sight for fireball"; the reply shows what was heard and a short answer;
  (2) type a question there; (3) at the table the DM says "hold on, I need to find if you need
  line of sight for fireball": the answer arrives privately, once a minute at most; (4) with two
  running games, a button asks which ("For <game>."); (5) the as-heard download has
  `[DM Sidebar id=… via=… stt=…]` and `(DMbot) [DM Sidebar reply-to=… model=… sources=…]` lines
  (everyone can read them); the cleaned download and the live transcript channel do not. A
  player who sends DMbot a message gets nothing. Core logs no ERROR.

